# Neo LFO parameters (docs/specs/neo-patch.md §3). The order is permanent: songs and presets store values by position.
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLfo
namespace NeoBuzz.LfoMachine
class NeoLfoMachine
summary A low-frequency oscillator that moves other machines' parameters: up to 8 targets (any parameter of any machine), each with its own depth, polarity, range and curve, written smoothly and never as an undo step. Seven shapes, a free rate in Hz or a tempo-synced one from 8 bars to 1/64 (straight, dotted or triplet), a phase offset, retrigger on the beat, the bar or a note of a machine, and smoothing. Use it for wobble, filter sweeps, tremolo, vibrato and slow movement on any machine, effects included.

group Wave
Shape     "Shape"       0 6 0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square Smooth_random Sample_and_hold | The wave: sine, triangle, saw up, saw down, square, smooth random or sample and hold
    id shape
    how Chooses the wave the modulation follows; the two random shapes pick a new value every cycle, gliding to it or holding it.
    sound Sine and triangle sway smoothly, saws ramp, square flips between two values, smooth random drifts, sample and hold steps.
Rate      "Rate"        0 1000 515 freq 0.02 40                | Cycles per second when Sync is Free
    id rate
    how Sets how fast the wave repeats, from 0.02 to 40 Hz, while Sync is Free.
    sound A low rate is a slow drift, around 5 Hz is a wobble or vibrato, higher is a fast flutter.
Sync      "Sync"        0 10 0   enum Free 8_bars 4_bars 2_bars 1_bar 1/2 1/4 1/8 1/16 1/32 1/64 | Free: Rate in Hz. Otherwise one cycle lasts this long at the song's tempo
    id sync
    how Locks one cycle to a length of the song's tempo, from 8 bars down to 1/64; Free uses Rate in Hz.
    sound Synced movement stays in time with the music and lines up with the beat.
Feel      "Feel"        0 2 0    enum Straight Dotted Triplet  | Straight, dotted (1.5 times longer) or triplet (two thirds as long) when Sync is on
    id feel
    how Stretches a synced cycle to 1.5 times (dotted) or shrinks it to two thirds (triplet); it only counts while Sync is on.
    sound Dotted and triplet cycles give the movement a lilting, off-grid pulse against the beat.
Phase     "Phase"       0 360 0  lin 0 360 ° 0                 | Where in the cycle it starts, and the offset when locked to the song
    id phase
    how Shifts the wave forward by 0 to 360 degrees of a cycle.
    sound Two LFOs at different phases peak at different moments, so their targets move apart.

group Behaviour
Retrigger "Retrigger"   0 3 0    enum Free Beat Bar Note       | Free: runs on. Beat or Bar: restarts the cycle each beat or bar. Note: restarts when the listened machine plays a note
    id retrigger
    how Restarts the cycle each beat, each bar or on each note of the machine it listens to; Free lets it run on.
    sound Retriggered movement starts from the same point every time, so every note or bar gets the same sweep.
Smooth    "Smooth"      0 1000 0 pct                           | Rounds the corners of the output (a one-pole of up to half a second)
    id smooth
    how Rounds off the wave's corners with a lag of up to half a second.
    sound Square and random shapes glide between their values instead of jumping; a high setting also shrinks fast waves.
Glide     "Write glide" 0 1000 492 time 0.001 1                | Time a target takes to cross its whole range: no write moves further than this allows
    id glide
    how Limits how fast a target may move: it takes at least this long to cross its whole range.
    sound A short glide keeps fast modulation clean; a long one smooths it into a slow drift and blunts fast waves.
